WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.120
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:04.640
I don't really want to make a video today, but it's Tuesday, so.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.680
Hank, when we were growing up in Orlando, Florida

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:09.560
It always felt to me like we were all just visiting

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.540
Like we were all just there for the theme parks

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:13.680
whether to visit them or work in them.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.860
And even today, when people ask me where I'm from,

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:19.560
I usually say Alabama, even though I didn't move there until I was 14

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.020
For a long time I believed that because I never felt fully at home in Orlando,

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.440
that no one else could either, but of course that's just

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.760
narcissism. In the 24 years since I have left

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.740
Orlando has become a great city

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:32.180
People have made it an awesome home town by growing

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:35.040
deep roots there - including a strong Latino community

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.960
and a vibrant LGBT community.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:39.220
Both of which have achieved so much with love,

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:41.840
and activism in the face of a long history of

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:43.440
violence and discrimination.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:48.020
And now, 49 people, killed in a gay club in Orlando.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:52.020
I-I don't know, Hank. I don't know what to say

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:54.620
I don't know if I have anything constructive to say.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.480
I do think it's valuable to listen to people who've been directly affected

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:58.660
by the shootings in Orlando.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.240
I've put some reading in the doobly-doo.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:03.220
I was particularly moved by the partner of Leroy Valentin Fernandez

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:05.200
who wrote: "You will always be my baby,

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:06.400
and I will always love you."

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.380
And by the brother of victim Amanda Alvear,

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:10.580
who said: "She wouldn't want anyone to spread hate for

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:12.720
her, she would want them to spread more love."

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.040
And by victim Luis Wilson-Leon's friend Daniel,

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.920
who said: "He'd been dealing with hate all his life.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:19.380
We all have. I have.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.440
He never retaliated with hate."

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:22.900
Aside from that, Hank, I really just want to share

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:24.460
with you the names of the people who were murdered.

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:26.480
I think we should hear their names as much as possible.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:28.820
Last night Orlando showed what a great city it is when

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:31.500
thousands of people came our to memorialize the dead

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:33.780
and to stand with their friends and families.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:35.960
Let us also stand with them, by listening to them,

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:38.240
by listening to those who loved them,

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:39.280
and by remembering them.

